<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- gameapp/GameApp.entitlements: the app's entitlements, applied to BOTH build shapes (gameapp/build_gameapp.sh).
     (No double hyphen may appear inside this comment: the SDK's parser and plistlib refuse it. docs/DECISIONS.md trap 14.)

     com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit raises this process's per-process memory ceiling. The
     rewrite peaks near 3.5 GiB resident in one process (docs/GAME-APP.md section 4), and jetsam is what decides
     whether that survives on hardware, so the app asks for the raised limit.

     WHERE IT HAS TO BE FOR IT TO TAKE EFFECT: the entitlement must be in the app's OWN signature (this file,
     embedded at signing time) AND the provisioning profile the installer signs with must also carry it. iOS
     honours the entitlement only when both agree. With a free Apple ID signed through SideStore or AltStore the
     profile is a personal development profile and may not carry it at all, in which case the app runs with the
     ordinary limit and this key changes nothing. The ONLY proof it was applied is os_proc_available_memory():
     it rises on the same device, or the entitlement did not take. The app prints that number at launch and
     around every heavy step (docs/PROFILE-DERIVED.md).

     com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing gives the process a much larger ADDRESS SPACE (not more
     RAM). At a 3364 MiB ceiling the census before the dlopen found 0.25 GB of free addresses and the guest block had
     to be squeezed (docs/STATE-GAMEAPP.md section 4); a Switch game reserves a large guest range. Same rule as above:
     the installer's profile must carry it too, which a developer account's App ID with the capability does.

     No secret, key or certificate lives here: entitlements are a plist, and the signing identity is the
     installer's, read from the Keychain at run time (gameapp/gameapp_shim.c). -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
